Top-p does not fix the number of candidate tokens: sort the probabilities from high to low, choose the **smallest candidate set whose cumulative probability reaches the threshold p**, and sample from those candidates. When the model is confident about the next token, a few tokens reach the threshold; when several candidates are plausible, more are kept.

Write a function `top_p_count(probs, p)`:

- `probs` is a probability list already **sorted from highest to lowest**;
- return the smallest number of candidates needed for the cumulative probability to reach `p`;
- the cumulative probability is judged **after adding the current candidate**, so the last candidate added always counts -- even if adding it pushes the total past `p`;
- when `p >= 1`, return `len(probs)`.

